### Generated by game/extract.py + build_graph.py — Pages CI rebuilds these on every deploy ###
src/main/java/com/rutik/systemdesign/game/questions/*.json
src/main/java/com/rutik/systemdesign/game/graph/*.json
src/main/java/com/rutik/systemdesign/game/case_questions/*.json
# The technology knowledge bank. Its SOURCE is technologies/tech_bank/*.md; extract.py
# parses those into this file. It was committed only because deriving a tool's roles
# needed a judgement pass — that judgement lives in the markdown now.
# NOTE: this file is still tracked from before the migration. Untrack it once with
#   git rm --cached src/main/java/com/rutik/systemdesign/game/tech_index.json
src/main/java/com/rutik/systemdesign/game/tech_index.json

### Android APK build — assets/ is regenerated by scripts/build_android_assets.sh; keystores never committed ###
android/app/src/main/assets/
android/.gradle/
android/local.properties
android/app/build/
*.keystore
*.jks

# Pre-rendered Mermaid diagram assets — regenerated by CI (scripts/build_diagrams.mjs), never committed
src/main/java/com/rutik/systemdesign/game/diagrams/

# Bundled iconify icon packs for Mermaid icon nodes — regenerated by CI (scripts/build_icons.mjs), never committed
src/main/java/com/rutik/systemdesign/game/vendor/icons-*.json

# CI build tooling (Puppeteer for diagram pre-rendering) — never committed
node_modules/

# Python bytecode from the build scripts (extract.py imports)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Throwaway per-session dev scripts. The convention is a leading underscore: a probe
# written to answer one question during one session, kept out of the tree so it cannot
# rot into something a future reader mistakes for tooling. Anything worth keeping loses
# the underscore and gets committed — see scripts/check_render.mjs, which root CLAUDE.md
# tells authors to run and which sat untracked for a day as a result.
scripts/_*.mjs
